{
  "id": "js-score",
  "name": "02 Score jobs",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## 02 Score jobs\nStarted by the scheduler (workflow 00), by default every 30 minutes: retires expired jobs, claims unscored jobs, asks Claude to score each against your profile, then validates and stores the result.\n\n**The model only reports.** The score, verdict and what happens next are computed by the scraper service (see docs/scoring.md). An invalid reply is counted and retried later; an API error is not.\n\n- **Model and batch size are settings:** `scripts/jobsearch schedule set score --model ... --batch ...`; the *Settings* node reads them.\n\n**Spending is capped.** Before each batch the service reserves the worst-case cost and only claims as many jobs as the monthly and daily caps allow (see docs/budget.md). At a cap this workflow simply does nothing.\n**If Claude does not answer** (an outage), the job's claim is handed back, so an outage never uses up a job's attempts.\n\n**Credentials needed:** a *Header Auth* credential named **Anthropic API key** (Name: `x-api-key`, Value: your key). See docs/workflows.md.",
        "height": 370,
        "width": 420,
        "color": 7
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -120,
        -440
      ],
      "id": "3b89d168-0d8a-5c03-92db-4aef99403c71",
      "name": "Notes"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "GET",
        "url": "http://scraper:8000/schedule/score/settings",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 60000
        }
